        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jimmy Hoffa, Jack Nicholson, Danny DeVito, David Mamet, John Joseph Nicholson, Karen Black, Susan Anspach, Ralph Waite, Sally Struthers, Robert Ciaro\n- Works: Hoffa, Five Easy Pieces\n- Organizations: Teamsters\n- Topics: biographical crime films, casting\n\nFacts:\n- John Joseph Nicholson was born on April 22, 1937, and he is an American actor and filmmaker who has performed for over 60 years.\n- Hoffa is a 1992 French-American biographical crime film directed by Danny DeVito and written by David Mamet.\n- Hoffa is based on the life of Teamsters leader Jimmy Hoffa.\n- In Hoffa, Jack Nicholson plays Jimmy Hoffa.\n- In Hoffa, Danny DeVito plays Robert Ciaro, a character that amalgamates several Jimmy Hoffa associates over the years.\n- Five Easy Pieces stars Jack Nicholson.\n- Five Easy Pieces features Karen Black, Susan Anspach, Ralph Waite, and Sally Struthers in supporting roles.",
